    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p>Bug Type: Visual / Animation<br/>
Priority: Low</p>

<p>Preconditions:</p>

<ul>
	<li>Game is running.</li>
	<li>Miya is selected and the player is in gameplay.</li>
</ul>


<p>Steps to Reproduce:</p>

<ol>
	<li>Select Miya on the Character Select screen and start the game.</li>
	<li>Aim the mouse in any direction.</li>
	<li>Press the left mouse button to shoot an arrow.</li>
	<li>Observe where the arrow appears and starts moving.</li>
</ol>


<p>Expected Result:</p>

<ul>
	<li>The arrow appears 16 px from the character and flies straight toward the mouse cursor (TC-MI-02).</li>
	<li>The arrow visually leaves the bow.</li>
</ul>


<p>Actual Result:</p>

<ul>
	<li>Miya holds the bow and plays the shooting animation, but the arrow appears at her feet and flies from there.</li>
	<li>The arrow does not leave the bow.</li>
</ul>


<p>Test Case Result:</p>

<ul>
	<li>FAIL</li>
	<li>Related Test Cases: TC-MI-02 (Shoot arrow toward mouse), TC-MI-01 (Miya starting stats)</li>
</ul>


<p>Notes:</p>

<ul>
	<li>Likely the arrow’s spawn position or offset is calculated from the character’s origin (feet) instead of the bow position.</li>
	<li>Check whether the issue happens in all aim directions or only some.</li>
	<li>Check whether the wrong start point affects hit detection, for example when shooting at enemies close to Miya.</li>
	<li>Attach a screen recording.</li>
</ul>

            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
